1. Specification-driven implementations
---------------------------------------

The following implementations are intended to follow published format
specifications or standards documents:

- DEFLATE: RFC 1951
- gzip: RFC 1952
- zlib: RFC 1950
- zstd: RFC 8878
- Brotli stream format: RFC 7932
- FastLZ: format behavior documented by the reference `fastlz.c`
  implementation (Ariya Hidayat, MIT license). Known-answer decode vectors
  in tests/integration/fastlz.rs were produced by running the reference
  encoder locally; no code was copied.
- LZRW1-A: format documented by Ross Williams' public-domain `lzrw1-a.c`.
  Known-answer decode vectors in tests/integration/lzrw1a.rs were produced
  by running the reference encoder locally; no code was copied.
- LZF: liblzf format documentation in `lzfP.h`/`lzf_c.c`
  (Marc Alexander Lehmann, BSD license) and the LZFFormat description
  (ning/compress wiki)
- Snappy: Google snappy `format_description.txt` (raw block format) and
  `framing_format.txt` (framed stream format)
- xz: `xz-file-format.txt` from Tukaani
- lzip container: GNU lzip manual
- LZMA-Alone `.lzma` container: `lzma-file-format.txt` from the XZ
  documentation (public domain)
- LZ4: LZ4 frame format specification
  (https://github.com/lz4/lz4/blob/dev/doc/lz4_Frame_format.md)
- tar: POSIX.1-2001 UStar / GNU tar extensions / POSIX PAX extensions
- cpio: POSIX `odc` / SVR4 `newc` / `newcrc`
- ar: IEEE Std 1003.1 (POSIX) ar format / GNU ar extensions / BSD ar extensions
- deb: `deb(5)` Debian binary package format (dpkg manual page,
  https://manpages.debian.org/unstable/dpkg-dev/deb.5.en.html)
- rpm: rpm.org Package Format documentation (format_v6 / format_header /
  format_lead, https://rpm-software-management.github.io/rpm/manual/)
  and rpm `lib/cpio.c` stripped payload behavior notes
- squashfs: SquashFS binary format documentation
  (https://dr-emann.github.io/squashfs/squashfs.html, CC BY-SA 4.0)
- mscab: [MS-CAB] Cabinet File Format documentation
  (Microsoft Open Specifications,
  https://learn.microsoft.com/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-cab/)
- xca: [MS-XCA] Xpress Compression Algorithm documentation
  (Microsoft Open Specifications,
  https://learn.microsoft.com/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-xca/).
  Known-answer decode vectors in tests/integration/xca.rs are drawn from
  [MS-XCA] section 3 examples and from Windows RtlCompressBuffer output
  reproduced in Samba lib/compression test suite (GPLv3+); the vectors
  are byte-level test data only, with no code copied.
- zim: openZIM Wiki "ZIM file format" documentation
  (https://wiki.openzim.org/wiki/ZIM_file_format)
- mtree: FreeBSD mtree(5) manual page
  (https://man.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?mtree(5))
- warc: IIPC WARC 1.1 specification / ISO 28500:2009
  (https://iipc.github.io/warc-specifications/specifications/warc-format/warc-1.1/)
- zip: PKWARE APPNOTE.TXT 6.3.10
- 7z baseline container: `7zFormat.txt` / `Methods.txt` (LZMA SDK 26.00)

Where code or tests use constants/tables taken from these specifications, those
values are treated as specification material rather than as third-party source
code.


2. Reference implementations and de facto format definitions
-------------------------------------------------------------

Some formats do not have a single RFC-grade specification and are implemented
against de facto reference behavior:

- bzip2
  - Reference: bzip2 1.0.x reference implementation by Julian Seward
  - Repository scope: Rust reimplementation of the format and algorithm
    behavior; no upstream bzip2 source files are bundled in this repository

- LZW / Unix compress `.Z`
  - Reference: `ncompress` / `compress42.c`
  - Repository scope: Rust implementation of the historical Unix `compress`
    format behavior

- LZO / lzop
  - Reference: Linux kernel `Documentation/lzo.txt` (LZO1X bytecodes) and
    lzop source (`lzop.h`, `p_lzo.c`) for the lzop file format
  - Repository scope: Rust implementation of LZO1X-1 block compression and
    the lzop framing format

- rzip
  - Reference: upstream `rzip.samba.org` `.rz` container and chunk semantics
  - Repository scope: Rust implementation of the upstream container shape and
    token/chunk behavior
  - Provenance note: the long-range matching and chunk logic are implemented in
    Rust for this repository and are not shipped as upstream C source files

- lrzip
  - Reference: lrzip framing plus the crate's upstream-faithful shared rzip
    token/chunk layer
  - Repository scope: Rust implementation of the crate's supported `.lrz`
    subset and backend wiring

- BCJ filters (x86, PowerPC, IA64, SPARC, ARM, ARM-Thumb, ARM64, RISC-V)
  - Reference behavior: xz / 7-Zip / liblzma style branch/call/jump conversion
  - Repository scope: Rust implementations validated against known vectors and
    expected filter semantics for all supported architectures

- Delta filter
  - Reference behavior: xz / 7-Zip style byte-wise delta (distance 1..=256)
  - Repository scope: Rust implementation validated against known vectors

- ZIP Method 10 (PKWARE DCL Implode) (`src/archive/zip/dcl_implode.rs`)
  - Reference: Mark Adler's `blast.c` from zlib contrib directory
  - Reference license: zlib license (permissive, compatible with AGPL-3.0)
  - Repository scope: Rust reimplementation of the blast.c decompression algorithm;
    no upstream C source files are bundled
  - Provenance note: Huffman code tables (LITLEN_REP, LENLEN_REP, DISTLEN_REP) and
    algorithm structure are derived from blast.c's static arrays and decode logic


3. Public-domain or permissively licensed upstream material
-----------------------------------------------------------

- PPMd7 / PPMdH shared codec (`src/compress/ppmd/**`)
  - Original reference: the PPMd implementation shipped within the 7-Zip
    project, as documented in files such as `Ppmd.h`, `Ppmd7.c`,
    `Ppmd7Dec.c`, and `Ppmd7Enc.c`
  - Rust-side basis: `ppmd-rust` crate (https://crates.io/crates/ppmd-rust)
  - Upstream port license: CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0
  - Repository scope: adaptation of that upstream PPMd7 model to this crate's
    `no_std + alloc` style and 7z method integration

- ZPAQ (`src/compress/zpaq/**`, `src/archive/zpaq/**`)
  - Reference: Matt Mahoney's ZPAQ format, context-mixing model, and ZPAQL VM
  - Licensing note: upstream materials are commonly presented as public-domain
    or similarly permissive source material; confirm exact upstream notice when
    refreshing references or importing assets
  - Repository scope: Rust implementation of a low-level single-payload codec
    plus a multi-entry archive layer with crate-local journaling


4. Bundled tables and static assets
-----------------------------------

- Brotli dictionary-related tables (`src/compress/brotli/dictionary.rs`)
  - Scope: static dictionary lookup tables, transforms, and affix data used by
    the Brotli decoder
  - Intended provenance: RFC 7932 Brotli static dictionary semantics together
    with the corresponding upstream Brotli dictionary structure used to realize
    those semantics in code and data
  - Maintenance note: if these tables are ever regenerated or replaced, keep
    their provenance documented alongside the source update

- Cryptographic and checksum primitives (`src/util/`)
  - CRC-32 (IEEE, `crc32.rs`): clean-room Rust, polynomial from ISO 3309
  - CRC-32C (Castagnoli, `crc32c.rs`): clean-room Rust, polynomial 0x1EDC6F41
  - CRC-64/XZ (`crc64.rs`): clean-room Rust
  - SHA-1 (`sha1.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation of FIPS 180-4
  - SHA-256 (`sha256.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation of FIPS 180-4
  - AES-128/192/256 (`aes256.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation of FIPS 197;
    includes CBC and CTR modes for ZIP and 7z encryption
  - MD5 (`md5.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation of RFC 1321
  - DES / 3DES (`des.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation of FIPS 46-3;
    includes CBC mode for ZIP Strong Encryption
  - RC2 (`rc2.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation of RFC 2268;
    includes CBC mode for ZIP Strong Encryption
  - RC4 (`rc4.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation;
    stream cipher for ZIP Strong Encryption
  - Adler-32 (`adler32.rs`): clean-room Rust
  - XXH32/XXH64 (`xxhash.rs`): clean-room Rust implementation of xxHash
  - BitReader (`bitreader.rs`): clean-room Rust LSB-first bit reader
  - Range coder (`range_coder.rs`): clean-room Rust range coder for LZMA/PPMd
  - Scope: all are self-contained implementations with no upstream C/C++ source
    bundled. Validated against published test vectors or reference outputs.

- Format constants and lookup tables elsewhere in the repository
  - Scope: Huffman/FSE/checksum tables and other codec constants
  - Intended provenance: published specifications, de facto format documents,
    or clean-room Rust derivations validated by tests


5. Current non-goals and exclusions
-----------------------------------

- This file does not claim that every implementation is a direct code port.
  In many cases the crate implements published behavior in Rust without
  bundling upstream source files.


6. Maintenance guidance
-----------------------

When adding or substantially rewriting a format implementation:

1. Record whether it is spec-driven, informed by reference behavior, or adapted
   from permissively licensed/public-domain upstream code.
2. If static assets, generated tables, or ported logic are introduced, update
   this file in the same change.
3. Keep `docs/spec/` focused on conformance and tests, and keep this file
   focused on provenance and third-party notices.
